/
/ This is what the HELP loader loads, at the point
/ where it has just over-written "Formerly a KSF".
/ It thus JMPs to START.  The words after this are
/ two bytes per word, and the first three words are
/ "DCA I 7" (3407), HLT (7402), and the Load address
/ of the subsequent code - 1.  The first of these is
/ deposited at "Becomes DCA I 7", the second is
/ stored at location 6 (to halt after loading is
/ complete), and the third sets up the load address
/ for the remainder of the code.
/
*7
	5
START,	KSF
	JMP .-1/10
	KRB
	RTL
	RTL
	RTL
	DCA 5
	KSF
	JMP .-1/17
	KRB
	TAD 5
	DCA ./23	/ Becomes DCA I 7
	ISZ 7
	JMP START/10
	JMP 6
	JMP START/10	/ Formerly a KSF
/ HELP Loader remnants
	JMP .-1/27
	KRB
	SNA
	JMP 27
$
